### ============================================================
### ATTENDANCE MODULE — Complete API Reference & Test File
### Base URL : http://localhost:5000/api/attendance
###
### facultyId   = numeric user_id  OR  uvfin string (e.g. "VF-2024-001")
### attendance_id = numeric primary key of the attendance table
###
### attendance_period values: "daily" | "weekly" | "monthly"
###   ▸ daily   → faculty submits for a single day
###   ▸ weekly  → faculty submits for a date within a week
###   ▸ monthly → faculty submits for a date within a month
###
### Every record in `data[]` returns FLAT fields:
###   subject_id, subject_code, subject_name
###   course_id,  course_name,  course_code
###   semester_id, semester_number
###   section_id,  section_name
###   allocation_id, session_type, rate_per_hour
###   attendance_period, week_number
### ============================================================


# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║           SECTION 1 — MARK ATTENDANCE (POST)            ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

### ----------------------------------------------------------
### 1A. GENERIC — POST /api/attendance/
###     Accepts any attendance_period in body (defaults 'daily')
###     Also supports bulk array in the same request.
### ----------------------------------------------------------

### 1A-i. Single record (daily, explicit period)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/attendance/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "user_id": 3,
    "course_id": 1,
    "semester_id": 2,
    "subject_id": 5,
    "attendance_date": "2026-07-23",
    "start_time": "09:00:00",
    "end_time": "10:00:00",
    "hours": 1,
    "month": "July",
    "year": 2026,
    "attendance_period": "daily",
    "status": "Pending",
    "remarks": "Regular lecture"
}

###

### 1A-ii. Single record using uvfin as user_id
POST http://localhost:5000/api/attendance/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "user_id": "VF-2024-001",
    "course_id": 1,
    "semester_id": 2,
    "subject_id": 5,
    "attendance_date": "2026-07-23",
    "start_time": "11:00:00",
    "end_time": "12:00:00",
    "hours": 1,
    "month": "July",
    "year": 2026,
    "attendance_period": "daily"
}

###

### 1A-iii. Bulk array (two records at once)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/attendance/
Content-Type: application/json

[
    {
        "user_id": 3,
        "course_id": 1,
        "semester_id": 2,
        "subject_id": 5,
        "attendance_date": "2026-07-23",
        "start_time": "09:00:00",
        "end_time": "10:00:00",
        "hours": 1,
        "month": "July",
        "year": 2026,
        "attendance_period": "daily"
    },
    {
        "user_id": 3,
        "course_id": 1,
        "semester_id": 2,
        "subject_id": 6,
        "attendance_date": "2026-07-23",
        "start_time": "11:00:00",
        "end_time": "12:00:00",
        "hours": 1,
        "month": "July",
        "year": 2026,
        "attendance_period": "daily"
    }
]

###


### ----------------------------------------------------------
### 1B. DAILY — POST /api/attendance/mark/daily
###     attendance_date defaults to TODAY if omitted.
###     month + year are auto-derived from the date.
### ----------------------------------------------------------

### 1B-i. Mark today's attendance (attendance_date omitted → auto today)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/attendance/mark/daily
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "user_id": 3,
    "course_id": 1,
    "semester_id": 2,
    "subject_id": 5,
    "start_time": "09:00:00",
    "end_time": "10:00:00",
    "hours": 1,
    "status": "Pending",
    "remarks": "Morning lecture"
}

###

### 1B-ii. Mark a specific date's attendance
POST http://localhost:5000/api/attendance/mark/daily
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "user_id": 3,
    "course_id": 1,
    "semester_id": 2,
    "subject_id": 5,
    "attendance_date": "2026-07-22",
    "start_time": "14:00:00",
    "end_time": "15:00:00",
    "hours": 1,
    "month": "July",
    "year": 2026,
    "status": "Pending",
    "remarks": "Afternoon session"
}

###

### 1B-iii. Bulk daily records (array)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/attendance/mark/daily
Content-Type: application/json

[
    {
        "user_id": 3,
        "course_id": 1,
        "semester_id": 2,
        "subject_id": 5,
        "attendance_date": "2026-07-21",
        "start_time": "09:00:00",
        "end_time": "10:00:00",
        "hours": 1
    },
    {
        "user_id": 3,
        "course_id": 1,
        "semester_id": 2,
        "subject_id": 6,
        "attendance_date": "2026-07-21",
        "start_time": "11:00:00",
        "end_time": "12:00:00",
        "hours": 1
    }
]

###


### ----------------------------------------------------------
### 1C. WEEKLY — POST /api/attendance/mark/weekly
###     week_number is auto-calculated from attendance_date if omitted.
###     month + year are auto-derived from attendance_date if omitted.
### ----------------------------------------------------------

### 1C-i. Single weekly record (week_number auto-calculated)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/attendance/mark/weekly
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "user_id": 3,
    "course_id": 1,
    "semester_id": 2,
    "subject_id": 5,
    "attendance_date": "2026-07-21",
    "start_time": "09:00:00",
    "end_time": "10:00:00",
    "hours": 1,
    "status": "Pending",
    "remarks": "Week 30 lecture"
}

###

### 1C-ii. Weekly with explicit week_number
POST http://localhost:5000/api/attendance/mark/weekly
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "user_id": 3,
    "course_id": 1,
    "semester_id": 2,
    "subject_id": 5,
    "attendance_date": "2026-07-21",
    "start_time": "11:00:00",
    "end_time": "12:00:00",
    "hours": 1,
    "week_number": 30,
    "month": "July",
    "year": 2026
}

###

### 1C-iii. Bulk weekly records
POST http://localhost:5000/api/attendance/mark/weekly
Content-Type: application/json

[
    {
        "user_id": 3,
        "course_id": 1,
        "semester_id": 2,
        "subject_id": 5,
        "attendance_date": "2026-07-20",
        "start_time": "09:00:00",
        "end_time": "10:00:00",
        "hours": 1
    },
    {
        "user_id": 3,
        "course_id": 1,
        "semester_id": 2,
        "subject_id": 6,
        "attendance_date": "2026-07-22",
        "start_time": "14:00:00",
        "end_time": "15:00:00",
        "hours": 1
    }
]

###


